This is a very creative and highly modified version of the first quarter of **Charles Dickens's classic novel, *David Copperfield***. 

It follows the exact plot, structure, and even the dialogue of the original book, but almost all of the character names and some locations have been swapped out. For example:
*   **David Copperfield** is now **Tiberius Kayla** (also called Davy, and later "Trot").
*   **Betsey Trotwood** (the formidable great-aunt) is now **Miss Rosie Sid**.
*   **Clara Peggotty** (the beloved nurse) is now **Bea**.
*   **Mr. and Miss Murdstone** (the cruel step-father and his sister) are now **Mr. and Miss Brevin**.
*   **James Steerforth** (the charismatic, privileged schoolboy) is now **J. Kyra**.
*   **Tommy Traddles** (the boy who draws skeletons) is now **Kourtney Isaiah**.
*   **Mr. and Mrs. Micawber** (the financially struggling landlords) are now **Mr. and Mrs. Sylvia**.
*   **Uriah Heep** (the "cadaverous" clerk) is now **Bradford Thomasina**.
*   **Mr. Wickfield** (the lawyer in Canterbury) is now **Mr. Cristal**.
*   **Blunderstone, Suffolk** (David's birthplace) has been humorously changed to **Kuala Lumpur, Selangor** (though still somehow in Suffolk!).

**Summary of the Plot Provided:**
The story covers Tiberius's (Davy's) birth and early idyllic childhood with his widowed mother and nurse, Bea. This peace is shattered when his mother marries the abusive Mr. Brevin, who brings his equally cruel sister to live with them. After Davy bites Mr. Brevin during a beating, he is sent away to Salem House, a miserable school run by the tyrannical Mr. Creakle. While there, his mother passes away. Davy is pulled from school and sent to do grueling manual labor at a wine-bottling warehouse in London, lodging with the perpetually debt-ridden Sylvia family. Eventually, he runs away, endures a brutal journey on foot to Dover, and throws himself on the mercy of his eccentric great-aunt, Miss Rosie Sid. She takes him in, chases away the Brevins, and takes him to Canterbury to arrange for his proper schooling, leaving him to board with her lawyer, Mr. Cristal.

